package legal

templ TermsOfService() {
	<article>
		<header>
			<h1>Terms of Service</h1>
			<p>Effective date: May 28, 2026</p>
		</header>
		<section>
			<h2>1. Service</h2>
			<p>Conex lets account holders create, manage, and publish simple websites under Conex-hosted paths. Some site management features require an account and an active session.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>2. Accounts and access</h2>
			<p>You are responsible for the email address used to access your account and for all activity that occurs through your account. Conex may send one-time verification codes to authenticate access and account changes.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>3. User content</h2>
			<p>You keep ownership of the site names, tags, and HTML content you submit. You grant Conex permission to store, process, display, and serve that content as needed to operate the service.</p>
			<p>You must not submit content that is illegal, infringes rights, contains malware, attempts to abuse the platform, or violates another person's privacy or security.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>4. Published sites</h2>
			<p>Sites may be private or public depending on their stored status. Public sites can be viewed by anyone with the site URL. You are responsible for reviewing content before making a site public.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>5. Plans and availability</h2>
			<p>Conex may offer free or paid plans with different limits and renewal terms. We may change, suspend, or discontinue features when needed to maintain or improve the service.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>6. Account deletion</h2>
			<p>You may delete your account through the service. Deleting an account removes the account and its sites from active use, subject to backups, logs, legal obligations, and operational retention.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>7. Disclaimers and liability</h2>
			<p>The service is provided as is and as available. To the maximum extent allowed by law, Conex is not liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or for lost data, profits, or business opportunities.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>8. Changes</h2>
			<p>We may update these terms. Continued use of Conex after an update means you accept the updated terms.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>9. Contact</h2>
			<p>Questions about these terms can be sent to the operator of Conex through the support or contact channel provided for the service.</p>
		</section>
	</article>
}

templ PrivacyPolicy() {
	<article>
		<header>
			<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
			<p>Effective date: May 28, 2026</p>
		</header>
		<section>
			<h2>1. Information we collect</h2>
			<p>Conex collects information you provide, including your email address, site paths, site names, tags, and site HTML. The service also creates account, login, email-change, plan, subscription, and session records needed to operate account features.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>2. Authentication information</h2>
			<p>When you log in or request an email change, Conex stores temporary verification request data and sends one-time codes by email. Access and refresh tokens are issued so clients can authenticate API requests.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>3. Usage and technical data</h2>
			<p>Conex may process request metadata such as IP address, user agent, requested URL, response status, and timestamps in server logs, security systems, and operational monitoring.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>4. How we use information</h2>
			<p>We use information to provide accounts, authenticate users, send verification email, create and serve sites, manage subscriptions, protect the service, troubleshoot problems, and comply with legal obligations.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>5. Public content</h2>
			<p>Public sites are available to anyone who visits their URL and may be indexed, archived, shared, or copied by third parties. Do not publish personal or confidential information unless you intend it to be public.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>6. Service providers</h2>
			<p>We may use infrastructure, database, email, logging, and hosting providers to operate Conex. These providers process information only as needed to provide their services to Conex.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>7. Retention</h2>
			<p>We keep account and site information while your account exists or as needed to provide the service. Temporary verification data, tokens, backups, and logs may be retained for limited operational, security, or legal reasons.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>8. Your choices</h2>
			<p>You may update your account email, update or delete sites, and delete your account through the service. You may also stop publishing a site by changing its public status or deleting it.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>9. Security</h2>
			<p>We use reasonable technical and organizational measures to protect information, but no internet service can guarantee absolute security.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>10. Changes and contact</h2>
			<p>We may update this policy as the service changes. Questions about this policy can be sent to the operator of Conex through the support or contact channel provided for the service.</p>
		</section>
	</article>
}
